        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Fifty-Five',
            subtitle: 'The Irish Auction',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Fifty-Five (55) is an advanced, bidding-based variation of the Irish national card game Twenty-Five. Deeply rooted in rural Irish tradition, it is a descendant of the ancient game 'Spoil Five'. The game is famous for its intricate and 'arcane' card rankingsâ€”where the Five of Trumps is always the highest card and the Ace of Hearts is a permanent trumpâ€”and its unique requirement that players bid for the right to choose the trump suit.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Fifty-Five evolved from 'Maw' (16th century) and 'Spoil Five' (19th century). While Twenty-Five is the foundational version, Fifty-Five added the bidding layer to increase the strategic depth and scoring potential.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3 to 6 players. Usually played as individuals.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Standard 52ndcard deck. The Ace of Hearts is a special 'Perma-Trump'.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Standard 52ndcard deck. The Ace of Hearts is a special 'Perma-Trump'.",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Each player is dealt 5 cards in batches of 3 and 2 (or 2 and 3).',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
