          human: "Welcome to Fifty-Five, where Irish tradition meets high-stakes card play. Master the unique rankings: in red suits, Aces are low; in black suits, Aces are high. The Five of Trumps is the strongest card in the game. The Ace of Hearts is always trump. Bid smartly, lead strategically, and watch for the 'jink' opportunity to double your points.",
          ai: 'Game: Fifty-Five (Irish trick-taking auction). Setup: 3-6 players, standard 52-card deck. Each player dealt 5 cards. Bidding phase: players bid in multiples of 5 (5-30). Highest bidder chooses trump and leads. Card rankings: Trumps (5 high, Jack, Ace of Hearts, Ace of trump, K). Red non-trump: K-A (A low). Black non-trump: K-J-A (A high). Ace of Hearts always trump. Gameplay: 5 tricks. Follow suit if able. Scoring: 5 points per trick. Jinking: bidder winning first 3 tricks can jink (go for all 5) for 25 points (lose all if fail).',
